// Type-checking a `<script type="tutuca/script">` block against a schema.
//
// A package of its own because it is the first thing in the language that
// needs `statedef`. `tscript` is text in, AST out, and stays that way — it
// ships to a browser twice over and should carry nothing a parse does not
// need. Checking is what happens once a declaration meets the type it is
// about.
//
// The governing rule is `viewgen/check_state.mbt`'s, adopted unchanged:
// **unknown is not wrong**. A `$method` result, a `*dyn`, a bind this block
// cannot see and a child component's fields are all opaque, and an opaque
// value silences every check that would have been made of it. A checker that
// guessed would cost more in false failures than the real ones are worth —
// which is why almost every rule below is written as "when BOTH sides are
// known".
import {
  "marianoguerra/tutuca/tscript",
  "marianoguerra/tutuca/statedef",
}
